  "notes": [
    "Fuel labels are preserved verbatim. In older years, some annual-summary categories group fuels that the daily worksheets separate; summaries are returned as published, without reaggregation.",
    "Daily and interval quantities remain in MWh. Early daily headings explicitly label MWH; modern monthly sums divided by 1000 reconcile to the published GWh summaries. Summary quantities retain their source MWh or GWh scale.",
    "2010 contains literal 1/0/1900 0:00 strings; 2011 contains 1.00E and 6.00E. These yield energyMWh=None with sourceError preserving the text. Numeric zero and absent source cells remain distinct.",
    "2011 August includes four unlabelled zero columns per daily fuel row. They retain their one-based sourceColumn, blank sourceHeader and ending=None. DST1/dst1-style headers also have no inferred clock time.",
    "2017-2019 workbook dimensions understate their data. The shared workbook loader resets XLSX dimensions before streaming cells.",
    "The 2026 workbook currently has data through July 31. Future-month headers and blank summary cells do not establish future generation data.",
    "Nine original regression workbooks are retained unmodified inside fuel-mix-originals.zip. This fixture is included only in source distributions, not the installed wheel."
  ]
}
